WEBVTT

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.680
It's morning...

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.390
I have to go to work.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:55.760
<b>Revelation of Malice</b>

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.010
I'm impressed you can eat 
so much in the morning.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.690
One wouldn't be a proper Offensive 
Jushikiist if they couldn't eat this much.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:10.750
That's encouraging.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:14.650
I used to eat as much as you do.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.150
So...

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.840
You didn't call us here just to 
have breakfast with us, did you?

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.160
I'm sure you remember,

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:27.660
but today's the third day that 
the Great Magatsushiki promised.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:35.030
These are the spots where the Magatsushiki 
have emerged in the past month.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.670
They're scattered everywhere.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:38.520
Yes.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:42.000
So we expanded our investigation
 to all similar incidents

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.930
in the past six months.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:46.430
All this?

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.730
Not all of them are,

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:53.020
but we ought to assume that the evening party
has been in preparation for quite a while.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:59.480
Either way, it's a certainty that we'll 
be fighting those two Great Magatsushiki.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:03.200
But without knowing anything about 
the purpose of the evening party,

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.950
or the Jushiki they'll be using, 
there's nothing we can do.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.170
What makes the Magatsushiki such a bother

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:12.300
is that each one has unique
characteristics and abilities.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.740
It's hard to come up with a plan.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:19.680
We'd hypothesized in the past

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.480
that the Magatsushiki's very existence 
is itself a kind of Jushiki.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.470
It seems that that was correct.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:28.640
They're believed to have originated from 
somewhere in high-dimensional phase space,

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:33.480
the fundamental principle of Jushiki.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:36.490
They aren't creatures from our dimension?

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:41.320
For them to appear in our world,

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:46.330
they need to use something 
from our world as a medium.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:51.530
In other words, they're using something 
or creature from our world as a medium.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.430
Baron Janahn Ghalan,

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:04.390
this so-called "food" is quite fascinating.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:10.390
Whether it's steel or stone,
I couldn't tell the difference.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:18.020
Could we not be more quiet at the table?

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.010
Sit down.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:23.530
We aren't here to fight you.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:28.250
Now that we've begun the evening party,
 we won't defy the rules.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.820
As entities of information, 
rules are absolute to them.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:35.540
All right.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:39.550
I heard what you said.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:44.550
It seems you still haven't figured 
out the purpose of the evening party.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:49.550
I'll give you a hint.

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:53.430
The party itself is a giant Jushiki curse.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:58.440
If you want to stop the party, 
you'll have to defeat the caller.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:04:59.950
The caller?

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.520
Someone summoned you?

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:03.320
Who?

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:06.190
I can't answer that question.

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:10.830
We aren't yet the masters 
of our own destinies, either.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:16.080
The first move is to see 
through the law of the party.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:20.730
Therein lies your hell and your answers.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.100
Oh, right.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:29.850
Hold on tightly to the Eye
 of the Cosmos that you hold.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:37.710
Iegie.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:39.080
Get Jabeira.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.510
The Great Magatsushiki appeared.

00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:41.860
We're meeting up immediately.

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:46.330
Shall we go after them?

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:47.350
No.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:50.480
<i>I have urgent information.</i>

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:51.740
<i>How much do you want it for?</i>

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.750
<i>I've located the Aurora Hammer's hideout.</i>

00:05:57.220 --> 00:06:00.750
<i>The weapons dealer Parumuwei tipped me off.</i>

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:04.760
<i>Of course, by last night, he was a corpse.</i>

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:07.760
We're here.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:14.200
Wait.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.720
There might be some traps.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.740
I used Agane.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:18.640
We're fine.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:24.190
No, not even a dog can 
sniff out a sealed bomb.

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:27.370
I don't smell humans at all through that door.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:28.900
That's good enough.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:33.040
Hurry up.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:37.710
There's a Draken saying that dragons 
feast on the slowest one's ass.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.360
There's someone here

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:43.420
who ought to go meet his fiancée 
with as much haste as he speaks of.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.220
We should get going.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:04.860
Egurrd.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:08.000
Why are you here?

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:13.500
Were you not prohibited from being 
further involved in this situation?

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.590
Why should I care?

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:19.330
We don't take orders from Dragon's Jaw.

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:21.790
This encounter is more than a coincidence.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.720
What the hell?

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:35.350
Viscount Remedius.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:39.560
Thank you, everyone, for your warm welcome.

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:43.350
Zhuo Lu.

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:49.210
There's no point in attacking a 
three-dimensional optical display.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:58.490
Poor Remedius.

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:01.560
You were the closest thing to me.

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:09.370
I invited you here to pass 
on the words of Remedius.

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:10.590
His words, you say?

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:13.120
His death was inevitable.

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:15.230
Why do you think that is?

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:16.600
Don't say it!

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.220
Don't say it?

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:23.040
The truth that the anti-government
 organization, the Aurora Front,

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.520
which later became the foundation
 of the Aurora Hammer,

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:27.580
was in fact created by the Dragon Empire?

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:31.760
That's serious foreign interference 
in domestic affairs.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:34.190
The attack during the hostage exchange

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:37.740
was actually an attempt to cover up 
the Dragon Empire's own scandal.

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:41.740
No, that's not it.

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:46.910
If the Dragon Empire was plotting the 
overturning of the Dochetta administration,

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:51.980
Viscount Remedius and the Aurora Hammer 
would have indeed been helpful.

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:54.570
The viscount was a civilian,

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:57.430
which made it possible for him 
to hide the empire's scent.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:01.190
It makes no sense to want to eliminate him.

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:06.110
Why did the late Remedius

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:10.270
despise the Dragon Empire and
Rahzel so much that he'd risk his life?

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:14.200
Why could Dragon's Jaw not explain that?

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:16.960
That is what you should investigate.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:20.160
Dragon's Jaw should know the reason.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.340
Listen to Remedius's words.

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:27.420
Feel extreme hatred.

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:36.170
<i>By the time you watch this recording, 
I will already be dead.</i>

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:40.680
<i>But if it's to acquire the 
twin Jushiki warheads,</i>

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:42.810
<i>I'll offer my life.</i>

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:46.010
<i>The Jushiki that was born of my research,</i>

00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:49.740
<i>never to be initialized by anyone 
before it was sealed away.</i>

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:51.590
<i>The Jushiki of Ava Dorn.</i>

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:56.320
<i>I assembled an initialization
Jushiki that was incomplete.</i>

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:59.820
<i>In order to initiate it, it requires the 
Jushiki power of several dozen people,</i>

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:04.400
<i>as well as computational and Jushiki 
power comparable an Altar's.</i>

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:06.330
<i>It's prepared.</i>

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:07.660
<i>Ava Dorn...</i>

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:12.340
<i>The Jushiki weapon that connects 
the other world to this world.</i>

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:14.560
<i>There are two warheads.</i>

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:16.760
<i>They will be detonated at high noon today.</i>

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:19.710
<i>Their target is Rahzel Island.</i>

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:22.520
<i>This is a warning.</i>

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:26.730
<i>The Dragon Empire will halt 
Jushiki weapon exports immediately.</i>

00:10:27.130 --> 00:10:31.730
<i>This message is being sent simultaneously 
to Eridana City and the Empire.</i>

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:35.480
<i>But should even one person 
try to escape the island,</i>

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:38.740
<i>the warheads will detonate that very instant.</i>

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:43.110
<i>The worst betrayal in the world, 
the worst backstabbing...</i>

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:46.960
<i>I pronounce to Rahzel Company:</i>

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:49.250
<i>Die. Die.</i>

00:10:49.660 --> 00:11:09.520
<i>Die. Die. Die. Die. Die.</i>

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:36.820
<i>Die... Die... Die... Die... Die...</i>

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:40.050
<i>Go to hell!</i>

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:43.680
<i>That alone is my wish.</i>

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:47.310
<i>Taste the hell that I've 
passed on to Zhuo Lu!</i>

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:51.260
<i>You at Rahzel Company will receive 
the despair and suffering</i>

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:53.940
<i>that Naricia endured.</i>

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:01.610
What now?

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:03.480
There's no time.

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:08.170
Remedius's curse will 
obliterate Rahzel in just...

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:09.190
Get out!

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.040
Gigina...

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:13.280
That island...

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:14.520
Rahzel Company...

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:15.670
Jiv's there!

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:25.470
<i>Jivenya here.</i>

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.550
<i>I'm at Rahzel Company right now.</i>

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:30.060
<i>If you need anything...</i>

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:32.640
It won't make a difference 
how many times you call her.

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:35.840
If your woman's on that island,
 leaving a message...

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:36.810
I know!

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:39.820
Everyone on that island is a hostage.

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:41.190
Shit!

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:43.040
Why does this happen?

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:44.590
Why do I always...

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:45.570
Stop, Gayus.

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:48.000
I'm like a gear of hell.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:51.030
I get sucked in and sent to doom.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:54.960
I make what I think are the best decisions 
and end up with the worst results.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.080
Gayus!

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:02.280
I'm not as good with words as you are.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:07.160
But the past, including all of my decisions,

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:08.850
are my flesh and blood.

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:12.120
I can't pretend I didn't exist now.

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:14.280
That's way too trivialized.

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:15.400
I'm sure.

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:17.100
Gigina...

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:19.050
What would you do?

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:24.710
Speaking as a Draken, so long as there's 
a battle in front of me, I will face it.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:29.120
Speaking as myself, I'll repay my debts.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:30.440
That's all.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.000
Yeah.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.400
Let's repay our debts.

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:44.130
This is a top-secret experiment on 
the seventh-order metatheorem Jushiki,

00:13:44.980 --> 00:13:47.630
Ava Dorn, that was conducted
 thirteen years ago.

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:49.310
Seriously?

00:13:49.310 --> 00:13:51.510
They put a hole in the dimensions?

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:53.890
The problem is what happens next.

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:57.140
From enormous computational capacity...

00:13:57.840 --> 00:13:59.980
This is the Magatsushiki world.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:03.080
From the pits of chaos,

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:06.900
these wretched plague demons were summoned.

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:11.160
They're simple creatures, not even 
worthy of being called Magatsushiki,

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:13.230
but that makes them all the more terrifying.

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:14.910
No, this can't be...

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.290
Fifty-eight seconds after
 the initial plague demon infection,

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:27.170
its Jushiki causes cell death.

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:31.930
Then, after 113 seconds, the victim 
begins bleeding from every bodily orifice,

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:33.680
falling into a coma.

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:37.950
Finally, 137 seconds after infection,
 the victim dies.

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:40.190
There are no treatments.

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:43.880
The fatality rate is 100 percent.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:50.740
Ava Dorn has an effective radius
 of roughly six hundred merters.

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:54.200
If it were to be detonated 
above Rahzel Island...

00:14:55.030 --> 00:14:56.080
Say it.

00:14:57.780 --> 00:15:00.640
All 1,205 people on the island

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:04.420
would die after enduring hellish suffering.

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:08.400
Rahzel Company's facilities

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:11.770
are currently undergoing evacuations 
to outside of the city

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:14.330
under the pretense of emergency training.

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:15.840
Then the island...

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:18.960
We need to at least contact them
 and determine a response.

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:22.350
All communication and transportation 
to the island has just been cut off.

00:15:23.140 --> 00:15:24.760
Mayor's orders.

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:26.730
We police have no option 
but to oblige, either.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:30.240
So we're going to just abandon them?

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:35.870
We just need to hit it before 
the Jushiki warheads are launched, right?

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:39.870
No one would be sitting here 
if we knew where they were.

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:43.880
But that's the only way to save them.

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:49.160
Two hours until detonation.

00:15:55.160 --> 00:16:00.280
I don't know where you get the nerve to 
just sit on a chair during such a crisis.

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:03.740
It's <i>because</i> we're in such a crisis.

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:08.780
It looks like the staff evacuation 
is going well, at least.

00:16:09.810 --> 00:16:12.300
You could do a lot of smuggling right now.

00:16:14.050 --> 00:16:17.560
There's a specialist electromagnetics 
Jushikiist jamming it.

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:19.160
You won't get through.

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:21.290
<i>What's wrong, Gayus?</i>

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:23.040
<i>I've been getting a lot of messages.</i>

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:23.820
Jiv!

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:25.170
Where are you right now?

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:26.520
Where?

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:28.540
At Rahzel Island. Why?

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:29.800
Is something wrong?

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:34.220
Oh yeah, there's been some fuss about
people not being able to connect.

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:35.160
Jiv...

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:36.070
<i>What?</i>

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:39.310
Sorry about yesterday.

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:43.870
<i>No, I was being a terrible girlfriend, too.</i>

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:44.970
Jiv...

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:48.760
<i>What? What's wrong?</i>

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:50.810
Jiv...

00:16:55.190 --> 00:16:57.450
Just give me a moment.

00:16:58.290 --> 00:16:59.290
Gigina.

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:03.860
Couldn't we save Jiv with your flight Jushiki?

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:06.510
It's possible.

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:07.550
But...

00:17:07.550 --> 00:17:08.620
Please!

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:13.840
Are you serious?

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:16.840
Yeah.

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:23.020
I'll tell you one of the 
greatest of Draken sayings.

00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:26.760
"No one can tell apart

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:28.780
what comes out of one's mouth or asshole."

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:34.900
Don't accept the late Remedius's curse.

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:38.870
It's no different than a pile 
of dog shit on the roadside to us.

00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:45.300
And you must never accept 
the death of your woman.

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:50.760
Jiv, I want to apologize to you in person.

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:53.230
<i>What's gotten into you, Gayus?</i>

00:17:53.230 --> 00:17:55.260
<i>You're acting weird today.</i>

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:58.410
Let's eat out next Sunday.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:00.940
I found a place that serves delicious crab.

00:18:01.920 --> 00:18:05.080
Promise me, please, that you'll go.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:07.980
<i>I don't mind, Gayus, but...</i>

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:11.550
Are you sure?

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:12.670
Yeah.

00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:14.780
I don't care who I'm up against.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:17.110
I'm going to win this fight.

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:22.190
<i>First, assuming the late chells</i>

00:18:22.190 --> 00:18:25.910
<i>master Remedius set up a perfect board...</i>

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:28.810
<i>There are two Jushiki warheads.</i>

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:31.620
<i>The question is what the 
detonation condition is.</i>

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.800
<i>The Jushiki power of a large 
number of people, Jushiki power</i>

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:37.050
<i>and computational capacity 
comparable to that of an Altar,</i>

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:40.050
<i>which could be the core of alchemy Jushiki...</i>

00:18:40.460 --> 00:18:44.430
<i>Two keys to open two warheads...</i>

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:47.930
<i>The equation for completing 
the demon's Jushiki...</i>

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:53.230
No, wait.

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:54.570
That's right.

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:56.470
I got it.

00:18:56.470 --> 00:18:59.940
I know the final scene of this 
ridiculously silly incident.

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:05.830
It was Remedius that summoned 
Amupura and Janahn Ghalan.

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:08.120
He controls the Great Magatsushiki

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:10.990
and gathered enough people's Jushiki

00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:13.300
to initialize the Jushiki warheads.

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:15.370
And in the final act,

00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:17.770
the Great Magatsushiki 
themselves become the core,

00:19:17.770 --> 00:19:20.250
contributing to the warheads' 
detonation conditions.

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:24.220
They called this order of 
events "the evening party."

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:27.140
So the Ava Dorn is really...

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:30.390
If we don't find and destroy the warheads,

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:32.480
their initiation is inevitable.

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:37.480
But there was one thing that even the 
genius Remedius couldn't control.

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:40.600
That was the will of the Great Magatsushiki.

00:19:41.310 --> 00:19:45.310
They want to fight us in the 
evening party for the sake

00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:47.140
of their own entertainment.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:50.500
That's why they left us with a hint.

00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:54.680
The locations of the Magatsushiki emergence?

00:19:54.680 --> 00:19:55.880
What about them?

00:19:56.720 --> 00:19:59.630
Human-faced Magatsushiki 
appeared at Boshor Point.

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:02.320
Giant fangs at the dental clinic.

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:06.040
At Largonkin's office, 
Deacon Sarvey and a model castle.

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:07.920
At the zoo, an elephant.

00:20:07.920 --> 00:20:09.690
At the storage facility, a large bird.

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:11.520
That's right.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:12.880
That makes sense.

00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:14.900
I'm starting to get it, too.

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:15.760
Yeah.

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:20.040
The Magatsushiki emergences 
had a certain set of rules.

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:21.030
Rules?

00:20:21.390 --> 00:20:22.900
What rules?

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:31.330
When the pawn makes it to here, 
it becomes a dragon piece.

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:34.170
The key to winning the match

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:36.580
is to make the most powerful dragon.

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:41.630
I've heard that you've memorized 
every game you've played to date.

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:43.220
Is that true?

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:44.270
Yes.

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:46.520
Not only every move I've played,

00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:52.630
but I remember, in detail, 
everything I've seen, heard, or felt.

00:20:54.130 --> 00:20:55.980
That's a tragedy.

00:20:57.360 --> 00:21:00.550
<i>Indeed, that's a tragedy.</i>

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:07.110
You've abandoned humanity and 
become a dragon, Remedius.

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:14.000
The old chells pieces looked 
different from how they do now.

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:17.560
For example, the bishops we use now

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:19.820
used to be fangs and elephants.

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:22.500
The castle used to be a ship or a large bird.

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:26.880
I get that the Magatsushiki 
were chells pieces,

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:30.760
but how does that indicate the 
locations of the Jushiki warheads?

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:35.270
The evening party is an enormous 
chells match played out on Eridana.

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:39.900
The pieces—the Magatsushiki—
emerged according to those rules.

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:42.530
And the last move...

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:47.530
It'll be the famous move Remedius used to win

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:49.280
the continental championship.

00:21:49.880 --> 00:21:52.290
You have the answer, then?

00:21:54.720 --> 00:21:57.040
The white king 
who will be defeated in battle...

00:21:57.730 --> 00:21:59.860
is here, on Rahzel Island.

00:22:00.560 --> 00:22:04.460
And the black dragon piece putting 
the other player in check...

00:22:05.450 --> 00:22:07.110
is the Osedek Clock Tower!

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:11.370
There are two warheads.

00:22:11.370 --> 00:22:13.590
They will be detonated at high noon today.

00:22:13.990 --> 00:22:16.550
Their target is Rahzel Island.

00:23:51.170 --> 00:23:55.450
Oh, friend, do not seek eternal paradise.

00:23:55.840 --> 00:24:00.300
Drink up the realms of possibility 
and set sail into the sea of stars.

00:24:00.300 --> 00:24:04.360
For we can never become more than we are.

00:24:02.580 --> 00:24:05.080
<b>Guillotine of Spiders • Time of Snakes</b>
